# Google Cloud compute / GKE

## Gate

Use when the user asks about Compute Engine VMs, instance groups, or GKE
clusters/node pools. Prefer Google Cloud MCP; else `gcloud`.

## Defaults

1. Never invent instance name, zone, cluster, or location — list/resolve.
2. Read-only status is the default (list/describe/get-credentials is fine
   when triage is authorized).
3. Create / start / stop / resize / upgrade need an explicit verb naming
   the resource.
4. After GKE context is known, prefer `kubernetes` for pod/event/log
   triage inside the cluster.

## Refuse

- Do not delete VMs, disks, or clusters without `google-cloud-safety` and
  an explicit delete verb.
- Do not open firewall or expose ports beyond what the user named.
